          <div class="feat-b">
            <span class="kicker">Consumer jewelry, direct to customer</span>
            <h3>The brand had outgrown a stock mailer</h3>
            <p>Average order value had passed $300 while the packaging had not moved with it. Stock mailers crushed under courier handling, and the generic foam left an inch of air around each piece, and rings rattled their way to micro-scratches.</p>
            <p>The rebuild used a 1200 GSM magnetic rigid box, a 157 GSM soft-touch wrap, a molded EVA insert over black velvet and hidden N45 magnets.</p>
            <a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://www.leelinepackage.com/jewelry-packaging-case-study/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read the Full Case Study<Fragment set:html={arrow} /></a>
